<h1>buddy system</h1>
<p>
(algorithm)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A memory allocation strategy which recursively divides allocatable <a href="block.html"><em>blocks</em></a> of memory into pairs of adjacent equal-sized blocks called "buddies".
</p>


<p>
<em>Note:
This term is included to minimize confusion with a <a href="buddytree.html"><em>buddy tree</em></a>. After LK.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>

<hr>

Go to the
<a href="https://www.nist.gov/dads/">Dictionary of Algorithms and Data
Structures</a> home page.

